Adaptation (internal/cmdutil MaxAbsDiffF32): no upstream code is adapted; the
contract is inspired by the finding. Fak adopts upstream assert_close's shape
and NaN refusal (testing.py:16-17): a length mismatch or a NaN on either side
now returns +Inf instead of comparing only the shorter prefix and skipping
NaN. Fak extends the refusal to mismatched non-finite pairs (an infinity
against a finite value or the opposite infinity yields +Inf), unlike
upstream's zeroing of non-finite entries (testing.py:19-20); matching
same-sign infinities still compare equal.

