Adaptation (internal/gateway legacy /v1/completions prompt arrays): no
upstream code is adapted; the contract is inspired by the finding. Upstream
treats a list of prompts as one request per element (llm.py:119-141), so a
multi-prompt array is a batch, not one prompt. Fak's gateway route does not
serve batches, so it now refuses a string array of two or more prompts with a
typed 400 (error.code prompt_batch_unsupported) before admission and before
any stream preamble, instead of joining the prompts with newlines into one
completion. A bare string and a one-element array are served unchanged.

