Adaptation (internal/gateway legacy /v1/completions structured carriers): no
upstream code is adapted; the contract is inspired by the finding. Upstream
carries so_args on every request's SamplingParams (sampling_params.py:59,82)
and builds the structured-output matcher at enqueue (llm_engine.py:606-612),
while PR#119 drops logprobs without a word (sampling_params.py:63). Fak's
legacy /v1/completions route had dropped response_format and every
guided-decode carrier the same silent way; it now decodes the same ten
carriers as /v1/chat/completions, applies chat's ingress refusals before
admission and before any EP follower or stream preamble, and passes the
carriers to the planner. Native refusals therefore carry the same typed code;
on stream:true that code arrives as an in-band SSE error.
